cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software archive (Zenodo DOI below) and the associated paper (preferred-citation)."
title: "host_parasite_interactions: genome-scale metabolic modelling of host–parasite (malaria) interactions"
type: software
version: v1.0.0
date-released: 2023-10-23
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/EPFL-LCSB/host_parasite_interactions"
url: "https://github.com/EPFL-LCSB/host_parasite_interactions"
abstract: >-
  MATLAB pipeline (using matTFA, redGEM/redHUMAN and CPLEX) to reconstruct
  context-specific genome-scale metabolic models of the human hepatocyte and of
  Plasmodium falciparum, build an integrated host–parasite model, and perform
  host gene-essentiality analysis for parasite survival. Companion code for
  Maurizio, Masid et al., Nat Commun 2024.
keywords:
  - genome-scale metabolic modelling
  - host-parasite interactions
  - Plasmodium falciparum
  - malaria
  - hepatocyte
  - thermodynamics-based flux analysis
  - gene essentiality
  - Recon3D
